1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:01,033
<i> I told you already.</i>

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,533
<i> Just let me handle this,</i>

3
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:03,867
<i> evrything will be all right.</i>

4
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,767
<i>How did you manage
to get him arrested?</i>

5
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,300
<i> I just planted a gun in his ca.</i>

6
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:10,767
<i>You gave in just because
of his whim?</i>

7
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,600
<i> Honestly, I don't even recognie</i>

8
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:14,600
<i> the man I married anymore.</i>

9
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:15,933
<i>No one's going
to believe him now.</i>

10
00:00:16,067 --> 00:00:18,500
<i>Delgado has been a thorn
in our side for a long time.</i>

11
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:20,700
<i>I'm starting to doubt
what's been happening to yo.</i>

12
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,867
<i> That came from Orbos' widow.</i>

13
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,100
<i> This is from the gym.</i>

14
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:27,000
<i>I found a notebook
among Orbos' things.</i>

15
00:00:27,133 --> 00:00:30,300
<i>I have a feeling the numbers
written there</i>

16
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:32,300
<i> are the key to your freedom.</i>

17
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:35,367
<i>She mentioned to me
that she had evidence,</i>

18
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:37,833
<i>something that would prove
Miguel is innocent.</i>

19
00:00:37,967 --> 00:00:41,067
<i>A video, but she was still
looking for the flash drive.</i>

20
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,400
<i>What do we do, Peter? We realy
don't have any evidence lef.</i>

21
00:00:43,533 --> 00:00:44,633
<i> That was so important.</i>

22
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:45,767
<i> I lost it!</i>

23
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:46,867
<i> I'll handle this.</i>

24
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,067
<i>I'm doing something
to clear my name.</i>

25
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,133
<i>I'm getting help
from Boss Budol.</i>

26
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:53,867
<i>Your immaturity won't help
your father's case.</i>

27
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,500
<i>Just so you know, I have
evidence that can help dad.</i>

28
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,700
<i>I just really need to find
that flash drive.</i>

29
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:02,933
<i>A flash drive about the cop
who died in Bolagos.</i>

30
00:01:03,067 --> 00:01:05,200
<i>I'm sure a lot of people
would be interested in this.</i>

31
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,867
<i> Stop looking for that video.</i>

32
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,033
<i>And don't ever mention
this to anyone,</i>

33
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,567
<i>not even to your Uncle Diego
or your mother.</i>

34
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:13,567
<i> You're looking for an evidenc?</i>

35
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:14,867
<i> What is it, Joey?</i>

36
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:35,467
Oh, no, no.

37
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,800
We're editing a video
of Uncle Miguel in action.

38
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:42,467
The cases he solved,
the people he helped.

39
00:01:42,633 --> 00:01:44,067
Proof that he's kind...

40
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,567
and he is not a murderer.

41
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:54,600
Is that all, Joey?

42
00:01:54,733 --> 00:01:56,900
You know, Joey...

43
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:59,033
there's nothing wrong
with what you did.

44
00:01:59,167 --> 00:02:01,133
You're right, okay?

45
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:03,200
But that doesn't mean...

46
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:06,567
it will help acquit your father.

47
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:11,267
Joey, what your father needs
is a strong defense...

48
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,533
and that's what
I'm going to provide.

49
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,300
I'll help your father.

50
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:21,733
I'll do everything I can
to help Miguel.

51
00:02:21,867 --> 00:02:25,533
And I'll take care of you
while he's gone.

52
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:27,467
Thank you, Diego.

53
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:31,667
It's nothing, Clarissa.

54
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,700
I consider you all as family.

55
00:02:34,833 --> 00:02:36,867
I won't abandon you.

56
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:46,833
- All right, I'll do it.
- It's okay.

57
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,033
- I'll do it.
- Oh, Peter.

58
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:50,367
Who is that?

59
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,367
Hello?

60
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:54,667
Miss Beautiful?

61
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,267
Boy, is that you?

62
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,367
Yes.

63
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,300
Didn't you say I should call

64
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:03,000
if I found a heart-shaped USB?

65
00:03:03,133 --> 00:03:04,767
Did you find it?

66
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,433
No.

67
00:03:07,567 --> 00:03:08,533
Boy, come on...

68
00:03:08,667 --> 00:03:11,533
But I know who took it.

69
00:03:11,667 --> 00:03:13,267
It's Panot!

70
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,800
Who's Panot?

71
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:16,233
Don't delete it.

72
00:03:16,367 --> 00:03:17,633
Don't tell me you're going
to let him fool you.

73
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:18,967
It's obvious he's a junkie.

74
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,033
Just don't delete it.

75
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,200
I'll deal with him.

76
00:03:28,233 --> 00:03:30,000
Okay.

77
00:03:40,567 --> 00:03:44,433
<i>There's an important video
in this...</i>

78
00:03:44,567 --> 00:03:46,967
<i> about the cop who died.</i>

79
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:49,100
Just tell him it's mine, okay?

80
00:03:49,233 --> 00:03:51,567
Tell him to wait for me
because I'm coming to get it.

81
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:54,300
All right, Boy, thank you.

82
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:55,433
- Peter.
- What?

83
00:03:55,567 --> 00:03:56,833
Let's go, we need to leave.

84
00:03:56,967 --> 00:03:59,133
- Come on.
- Wait, wait, wait.

85
00:03:59,267 --> 00:04:01,100
What about your dad?

86
00:04:01,233 --> 00:04:02,800
This is for him, right?

87
00:04:02,933 --> 00:04:04,533
I mean, didn't uncle say

88
00:04:04,667 --> 00:04:06,733
we should stop finding
that video?

89
00:04:06,867 --> 00:04:08,500
He's right, you might get
yourself into trouble.

90
00:04:08,633 --> 00:04:09,633
We're so close
to getting the evidence.

91
00:04:09,767 --> 00:04:11,067
Are we really going to stop now?

92
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,867
Joey!

93
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,900
Are you two fighting?

94
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:17,867
No, Mom.

95
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,000
Sorry.

96
00:04:23,133 --> 00:04:26,067
I'm just really stressed
about what's happening to dad.

97
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,800
Mom, I'd like to stay,

98
00:04:27,967 --> 00:04:30,900
but I have to leave.
I still have class.

99
00:04:31,033 --> 00:04:32,567
Joey,

100
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:35,867
your father will understand
if you really need to go back.

101
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,933
You need to focus
on your studies.

102
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:42,400
Let us adults handle
this problem.

103
00:04:42,533 --> 00:04:46,100
I'm really sorry, Mom.
I'm leaving you alone.

104
00:04:46,233 --> 00:04:49,400
What are you saying?
I can take care of myself.

105
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:54,267
I may not be as fierce
as your father, but...

106
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,033
your mother is a strong woman.

107
00:04:57,167 --> 00:04:59,767
And I'll get through this
for you.

108
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,733
We'll get through this, Mom.

109
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:09,200
Even if we're not together,
we're still a family, right?

110
00:05:09,333 --> 00:05:11,400
I'll really pray that...

111
00:05:12,333 --> 00:05:14,567
this problem gets fixed...

112
00:05:15,767 --> 00:05:18,033
that you and dad will be okay,

113
00:05:18,167 --> 00:05:20,100
that our family
will be whole again.

114
00:05:21,267 --> 00:05:23,467
I'm praying for that too, Joey.

115
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:34,933
I'm sorry, Miss Beautiful,

116
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:39,467
but Panot won't give your USB
back for free.

117
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,600
What? But that's mine!

118
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:44,833
He's money-hungry!

119
00:05:44,967 --> 00:05:47,467
He said someone wants to buy it.

120
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,567
What?

121
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:49,667
Then I'll buy it myself.

122
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,833
I'm willing to pay.

123
00:05:50,967 --> 00:05:52,433
Joey.

124
00:05:52,567 --> 00:05:54,033
Where can I find this Panot?

125
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,667
Is he here at the market?

126
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,200
He eats here,

127
00:05:57,333 --> 00:06:01,733
but he guards a hollow block
factory over at District Three.

128
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:03,300
All right, thank you so much,
Boy.

129
00:06:03,433 --> 00:06:04,633
You've really helped me.

130
00:06:04,767 --> 00:06:06,867
Thank you for the food,

131
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,333
but please be careful
going to Panot.

132
00:06:10,933 --> 00:06:12,100
All right.

133
00:06:12,233 --> 00:06:14,333
- Thanks, Boy.
- Thank you.

134
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:19,500
Are you really
going to see Panot?

135
00:06:19,633 --> 00:06:22,733
I have to get my USB back.

136
00:06:22,867 --> 00:06:25,433
Can't you just buy a new one?

137
00:06:25,567 --> 00:06:28,500
It's very risky,
who knows what he might do?

138
00:06:28,633 --> 00:06:30,100
He's a junkie.

139
00:06:39,067 --> 00:06:41,000
It's my contact person
from the market, Madam.

140
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:43,367
Then answer it!

141
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:47,600
- Hello?
- Hello, Boss?

142
00:06:47,733 --> 00:06:49,767
That woman is back here
at the market.

143
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,833
Looks like she's searching
for something.

144
00:06:51,967 --> 00:06:54,267
All right.

145
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:55,700
What are you waiting for?

146
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:57,600
Hurry up! Go there now!

147
00:06:57,733 --> 00:06:59,100
Okay, Madam.

148
00:07:00,633 --> 00:07:02,300
Hurry!

149
00:07:07,033 --> 00:07:09,667
Clarissa doesn't want
to come here for now.

150
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:12,533
She said you might just argue.

151
00:07:12,667 --> 00:07:16,800
Your daughter Joey already went
back to the province.

152
00:07:16,967 --> 00:07:18,667
She said she has classes.

153
00:07:19,933 --> 00:07:24,300
Let it be, so they won't be
put in danger.

154
00:07:24,433 --> 00:07:27,100
Take care of my wife
and child for me.

155
00:07:27,233 --> 00:07:28,967
Watch over them.

156
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,900
You don't have to tell me that,
Miguel.

157
00:07:32,033 --> 00:07:34,733
That's automatic already, Buddy.

158
00:07:34,867 --> 00:07:37,300
And you too...

159
00:07:37,433 --> 00:07:39,767
don't visit here anymore.

160
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,767
You might get dragged into this.

161
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:45,167
The people I'm up against
are powerful.

162
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:48,233
They can fake my ballistics...

163
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,633
that's why
they're keeping me here.

164
00:07:52,467 --> 00:07:55,967
Then you really do need me here.

165
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:58,000
Don't worry, Miguel.

166
00:07:58,133 --> 00:08:00,967
I'll do everything,
I'll find out who's behind this.

167
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,967
- I'll help you.
- I'll handle the investigation

168
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,967
on my end.

169
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:08,033
How can you handle it?
You're locked up in here.

170
00:08:10,967 --> 00:08:13,967
Miguel, is someone helping you
from the outside?

171
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:15,867
Who?

172
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,333
I'll tell you...

173
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,467
once I'm sure.

174
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,867
Why, Miguel? Don't you trust me
anymore, Buddy?

175
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,633
I trust you.

176
00:08:27,767 --> 00:08:30,533
That's why I'm entrusting
my wife and child to you.

177
00:08:31,767 --> 00:08:33,667
Take care of them.

178
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,167
Tell them...

179
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,467
that once everything is fixed,

180
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,567
I'll come back for them.

181
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:56,400
I have a little savings,
around five thousand pesos.

182
00:08:56,567 --> 00:08:59,200
That should be enough
to get the video back, right?

183
00:08:59,333 --> 00:09:01,300
Joey, five thousand pesos?
Are you serious?

184
00:09:01,433 --> 00:09:02,867
You heard what the vendor said,
didn't you?

185
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,667
That Panot is dangerous.

186
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:08,033
What's dangerous is my dad
going to prison for life

187
00:09:08,167 --> 00:09:10,533
if we don't get
the evidence back.

188
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:14,500
But, Joey...

189
00:09:14,633 --> 00:09:16,900
Peter, I get that you're scared.

190
00:09:17,033 --> 00:09:18,500
But you don't have
to come with me.

191
00:09:18,633 --> 00:09:20,667
Just don't stop me.

192
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
<i>Do you have
a female worker here?</i>

193
00:09:27,133 --> 00:09:29,000
<i> We're looking for someone.</i>

194
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,067
Come on, let's go.

195
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,800
Joey, what are you going to...

196
00:09:39,933 --> 00:09:41,333
Are you still mad?

197
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,000
I just have a lot on my mind.

198
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,733
Joey, I'm just concerned
about you.

199
00:09:48,867 --> 00:09:50,533
It's dangerous to try
to take back that flash drive

200
00:09:50,667 --> 00:09:52,233
from that bald guy.

201
00:09:52,367 --> 00:09:54,000
And that's not all, there are
others looking for you too.

202
00:09:54,133 --> 00:09:55,767
- Right?
- I know!

203
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,333
But I can't just abandon
my father.

204
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,200
Peter, didn't I tell you?

205
00:10:02,367 --> 00:10:04,333
You don't have to come with me.

206
00:10:05,767 --> 00:10:07,233
Thank you, thank you
for all your help.

207
00:10:07,367 --> 00:10:09,767
But if this is as far
as you can go, it's okay.

208
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,400
I won't take it against you.

209
00:10:20,633 --> 00:10:22,067
Andrew, don't push through
with this.

210
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,967
I'm the one getting
worried about you.

211
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:26,100
What are you talking about?

212
00:10:26,233 --> 00:10:28,600
That's the exciting part
of our job.

213
00:10:28,733 --> 00:10:32,067
And I can take care of myself.

214
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,467
Oh, wow, that really
reassures me.

215
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:36,867
Right?

216
00:10:37,733 --> 00:10:39,467
Why are you so convinced

217
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:44,533
that the video that bald guy
is talking about is real?

218
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:46,367
What if he's just a hustler?

219
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,700
I just have a feeling
that this could be big.

220
00:10:49,833 --> 00:10:51,733
Okay, let's just say that...

221
00:10:51,867 --> 00:10:53,733
I have a credible source.

222
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,167
Okay, fine.

223
00:10:58,567 --> 00:11:00,033
You said it.

224
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:01,533
I'll see you.

225
00:11:09,267 --> 00:11:10,633
Peter...

226
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,467
Here.

227
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,800
That's five thousand
five hundred pesos.

228
00:11:20,733 --> 00:11:23,467
My savings from my shop salary.

229
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,033
To add to the payment for Panot.

230
00:11:26,167 --> 00:11:27,900
In case you run short on money.

231
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:30,967
Peter, it's not really
necessary.

232
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:32,533
I want to.

233
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:34,433
Okay? I want to, Joey.

234
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,233
The only reason
I stopped you earlier

235
00:11:37,367 --> 00:11:38,633
because I was concerned.

236
00:11:40,067 --> 00:11:42,200
But if you're going
through with this...

237
00:11:42,367 --> 00:11:44,300
of course, I'm coming with you.

238
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:46,700
I won't let you go alone.

239
00:11:54,767 --> 00:11:58,033
Sorry, Peter, for arguing
with you earlier.

240
00:11:59,333 --> 00:12:00,367
What you said was right.

241
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:02,600
What we're about to do
is dangerous.

242
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:06,033
But I need to be brave

243
00:12:06,167 --> 00:12:08,533
so I can fix my family again.

244
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:14,300
Thank you, Peter.

245
00:12:20,467 --> 00:12:22,300
That's going to happen soon.

246
00:12:22,433 --> 00:12:23,933
I believe it.

247
00:12:25,867 --> 00:12:27,333
Let's go.

248
00:12:33,933 --> 00:12:35,333
Ouch.

249
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:36,500
Let's go.

250
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:38,100
Thank you.

251
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:07,200
You still haven't found
the woman?

252
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:09,333
Useless fools!

253
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,733
Good for nothing idiots!

254
00:13:11,867 --> 00:13:14,300
They've probably left by
the time we got to the market.

255
00:13:14,433 --> 00:13:15,833
But we picked up
something, Madam.

256
00:13:15,967 --> 00:13:18,000
It's true, there's a video
of you torturing Ramon.

257
00:13:18,133 --> 00:13:19,767
How did you find out?

258
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:21,933
Some junkie wouldn't stop
talking at the market.

259
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:23,433
He said he's selling a USB

260
00:13:23,567 --> 00:13:26,533
containing a video of the late
Police Officer from Bolagos.

261
00:13:26,667 --> 00:13:28,600
So are you telling me...

262
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:30,767
more and more people
have seen the video?

263
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:32,000
What do you want to do, Madam?

264
00:13:32,133 --> 00:13:34,200
Pay them off or silence them?

265
00:13:35,533 --> 00:13:36,700
Most likely,

266
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:38,467
that's where the woman you're
looking for is headed too, Lisa.

267
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:55,233
In that case, I'll deal
with them personally.

268
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,067
Let's go!

269
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,700
This is it.

270
00:14:23,833 --> 00:14:26,333
This is the factory they were
talking about in District Three.

271
00:14:28,833 --> 00:14:30,267
Let's go.

272
00:14:31,267 --> 00:14:32,600
Don't be scared.

273
00:14:32,733 --> 00:14:34,167
I won't leave you.

274
00:14:36,867 --> 00:14:38,233
Three thousand pesos.

275
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,700
That's a loss!

276
00:14:45,833 --> 00:14:47,700
That's too low, Boss Idol!

277
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:50,600
- That's a loss!
- There are a lot of us here!

278
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,333
Raise it.

279
00:14:54,467 --> 00:14:56,233
Panot, someone's coming!

280
00:15:02,267 --> 00:15:03,967
What are you doing here?

281
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:05,733
You again?

282
00:15:05,867 --> 00:15:08,867
So Panot's selling
the flash drive to you?

283
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:31,100
Who are you?

284
00:15:32,233 --> 00:15:33,833
Why do you know me?

285
00:15:33,967 --> 00:15:35,533
That flash drive is mine,

286
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,467
and I really need it.

287
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:42,600
You're Boy's contact.

288
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:46,733
I'm not giving this for free.

289
00:15:49,367 --> 00:15:51,967
Of course, Mister, I'll pay.

290
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:53,933
Honestly, I'll even pay more

291
00:15:54,067 --> 00:15:55,733
than what Boss Idol's offering.

292
00:15:55,867 --> 00:15:57,267
How much is he offering?

293
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,867
Just three thousand pesos,
right?

294
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,533
I'll give four thousand pesos.

295
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:01,800
- There you go!
- There you go!

296
00:16:01,933 --> 00:16:03,600
- Higher!
- That works.

297
00:16:03,733 --> 00:16:04,533
How about you?

298
00:16:04,667 --> 00:16:05,700
Five thousand pesos.

299
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:09,100
- Boss, that's already good.
- That's okay, Boss.

300
00:16:10,133 --> 00:16:11,000
Six thousand pesos.

301
00:16:11,133 --> 00:16:13,133
- There you go!
- There you go!

302
00:16:17,467 --> 00:16:19,300
Seven thousand pesos.

303
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:23,400
You were so stingy earlier.

304
00:16:23,533 --> 00:16:25,933
Now you're pulling out cash?

305
00:16:26,067 --> 00:16:27,567
Ten thousand pesos.

306
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,467
- There you go!
- There you go!

307
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,833
- Boss, that's a win already!
- That'll do.

308
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:41,000
Joey, shouldn't it be nine
thousand pesos first?

309
00:16:41,133 --> 00:16:43,267
It's taking too long.
So it's quicker.

310
00:16:44,433 --> 00:16:45,867
So, Boss Idol?

311
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,267
Are you really going
to give them the win?

312
00:16:59,067 --> 00:17:00,733
What are you doing?

313
00:17:01,433 --> 00:17:02,467
Oh, why?

314
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,400
Are you short on cash?

315
00:17:04,533 --> 00:17:06,800
You thought you could
scam them too, right?

316
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:09,333
Joey, I'm serious.

317
00:17:09,467 --> 00:17:11,100
Don't waste your money here.

318
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:12,300
I'll buy the video.

319
00:17:12,433 --> 00:17:15,300
I'll use it for my program.

320
00:17:15,467 --> 00:17:17,933
If this really
is the evidence you claim.

321
00:17:18,067 --> 00:17:21,633
Then Major Delgado
will be acquitted

322
00:17:21,767 --> 00:17:23,800
once I reveal it to everyone.

323
00:17:23,933 --> 00:17:26,500
What if you change your mind?

324
00:17:26,633 --> 00:17:28,167
What if you bury the video?

325
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:30,233
Aren't you mad at the police?

326
00:17:30,367 --> 00:17:33,000
You've been targeting my father.

327
00:17:33,133 --> 00:17:34,733
Joey...

328
00:17:35,633 --> 00:17:37,467
I'm not like you.

329
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:40,233
I'm not as petty as you,
not as immature.

330
00:17:40,367 --> 00:17:43,733
I keep my word.

331
00:17:43,867 --> 00:17:45,000
Wait...

332
00:17:45,133 --> 00:17:47,167
aren't you the one
asking us for help?

333
00:17:48,467 --> 00:17:51,500
Why would we cooperate with you
if you're trash-talking Joey?

334
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,567
You're right about that, Peter.

335
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:58,767
Panot, ten thousand
five hundred pesos.

336
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:00,833
- There you go!
- There you go!

337
00:18:00,967 --> 00:18:02,500
If I were you, I'd take it.

338
00:18:02,633 --> 00:18:04,900
Looks like Boss Scam here
won't be paying anymore.

339
00:18:05,033 --> 00:18:06,767
- Go ahead!
- He's trying to scam you.

340
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:08,700
That could be.

341
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:10,200
Fifteen thousand pesos.

342
00:18:10,333 --> 00:18:16,400
- Take it, Boss!
- That'll do!

343
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:20,600
So, that's it?

344
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,933
Boss Idol wins!

345
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,067
Give me the money.

346
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,400
Flash drive first,
take it out.

347
00:18:44,833 --> 00:18:46,333
You see this?

348
00:18:46,467 --> 00:18:47,833
Is that really it?

349
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:58,300
Fifteen thousand pesos.

350
00:18:59,867 --> 00:19:01,833
Winner.

351
00:19:04,933 --> 00:19:06,533
It has to be hand-to-hand.

352
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,833
Hey.

353
00:19:08,967 --> 00:19:11,467
That's Boss Idol.

354
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:12,833
Game.

355
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:15,133
Hey!

356
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:24,500
Hey!

357
00:19:24,633 --> 00:19:26,600
You guys are messed up!

358
00:19:26,733 --> 00:19:28,933
We already had a deal earlier!

359
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:30,600
Just stay out of this.

360
00:19:30,733 --> 00:19:33,367
Aren't you two enemies anyway?

361
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,267
Let's go, Joey.

362
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:37,000
Give me that flash drive.

363
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,633
The woman is inside.

364
00:19:56,767 --> 00:19:58,133
She has two companions with her.

365
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:04,233
It's time to meet that freakin'
girl and get that video.

366
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,233
You don't want to?

367
00:20:12,367 --> 00:20:13,267
Joey!

368
00:20:27,033 --> 00:20:27,900
Hand it over.

369
00:20:28,033 --> 00:20:29,667
In your dreams.

370
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:33,733
Hey! Where do you think
you're going?

371
00:20:33,867 --> 00:20:35,467
This is solid as a rock, boy.

372
00:21:01,267 --> 00:21:03,167
You really don't want to?

373
00:21:03,867 --> 00:21:05,667
You wish!

374
00:21:47,833 --> 00:21:49,500
You seem worried,
is there a problem?

375
00:21:49,633 --> 00:21:51,900
It's Joey, she's not answering
my calls.

376
00:21:52,033 --> 00:21:54,233
My problem right now is Jin Ho!

377
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:55,900
- Stop!
- Jin Ho?

378
00:21:56,033 --> 00:21:58,133
He recognized me! He saw me!

379
00:21:58,267 --> 00:21:59,233
So, everybody, listen.

380
00:21:59,367 --> 00:22:00,833
You can't call anyone tonight.

381
00:22:00,967 --> 00:22:02,967
Jin Ho won't stop
coming after me.

382
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:04,767
- Your gun.
- My gun, here.

383
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:08,633
Focus on Berdugo's order,
kill Delgado.

384
00:22:08,767 --> 00:22:11,900
What if this is connected
to your father's case?

385
00:22:12,033 --> 00:22:12,600
I knew it.

386
00:22:12,733 --> 00:22:13,633
You were just pretending

387
00:22:13,767 --> 00:22:15,467
when you said
you trusted that Jin Ho.

388
00:22:15,633 --> 00:22:17,533
Please don't kill us.
It's his fault.

389
00:22:17,667 --> 00:22:20,433
Keep her out of this.

390
00:22:20,567 --> 00:22:23,900
Did you ask your men
if they saw a flash drive?

391
00:22:25,367 --> 00:22:26,367
What are you hiding?

392
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:28,700
That's the only way
I can find out who did this.

393
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:30,067
Impossible.
